  "aiContextParagraph": "On November 12, 2026, Gibran Rakabuming Raka officially resigned from his role as the Vice President of Indonesia. Following a formal meeting with President Prabowo Subianto at the Merdeka Palace to submit his resignation, the former vice president was seen departing the official residence after bidding farewell to staff and volunteers. In response to the vacancy, President Prabowo Subianto has initiated meetings with leaders from the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) and the House of Representatives (DPR) to discuss the necessary parliamentary procedures for electing a new vice president. As these administrative discussions unfold, the Presidential Palace has also seen preparations involving the arrival of local food vendors, while officials continue to manage the logistics of the leadership transition process. The government has prioritized finalizing the schedule for the required plenary session to ensure institutional stability.",
